(function(E){ const x = E["exam-06"] = E["exam-06"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x06-l2"] = {"id":"x06-l2","patterns":["L2-volunteer"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 2: volunteer roles","tr":"Listening Part 2: gönüllü görevleri","fa":"Listening Part 2: نقش‌های داوطلبانه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match each part of a talk to the right option in a box of nine, using each letter once, and then answer A-C questions about practical information.","tr":"Bu derste bir konuşmanın her bölümünü dokuz seçenekli bir kutudaki doğru seçenekle, her harfi bir kez kullanarak eşleştirmeyi ve sonra pratik bilgilerle ilgili A-C sorularını cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری هر بخش از یک صحبت را با گزینه‌ی درست از یک کادر نُه‌تایی جور کنی، طوری که هر حرف یک بار به کار برود، و بعد به سؤال‌های A-C درباره‌ی اطلاعات عملی جواب بدهی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 2: volunteer roles","tr":"Listening Part 2: gönüllü görevleri","fa":"Listening Part 2: نقش‌های داوطلبانه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match each part of a talk to the right option in a box of nine, using each letter once, and then answer A-C questions about practical information.","tr":"Bu derste bir konuşmanın her bölümünü dokuz seçenekli bir kutudaki doğru seçenekle, her harfi bir kez kullanarak eşleştirmeyi ve sonra pratik bilgilerle ilgili A-C sorularını cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری هر بخش از یک صحبت را با گزینه‌ی درست از یک کادر نُه‌تایی جور کنی، طوری که هر حرف یک بار به کار برود، و بعد به سؤال‌های A-C درباره‌ی اطلاعات عملی جواب بدهی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"1"},{"label":{"en":"Options in the box","tr":"Kutudaki seçenek","fa":"گزینه‌های کادر"},"value":"A-I"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: volunteering at a library","tr":"Bu sınav: bir kütüphanede gönüllülük","fa":"این آزمون: داوطلبی در یک کتابخانه"},"intro":{"en":"Part 2 is one person giving information to a group. Volunteering talks come up regularly: an organiser lists the roles and then the practical steps. The roles come in the same order as the questions.","tr":"Part 2, bir gruba bilgi veren tek bir kişidir. Gönüllülük konuşmaları düzenli olarak çıkar: bir organizatör görevleri sıralar, sonra pratik adımları anlatır. Görevler sorularla aynı sırada gelir.","fa":"Part 2 یک نفر است که به یک گروه اطلاعات می‌دهد. صحبت‌هایی درباره‌ی داوطلبی مرتب می‌آیند: برگزارکننده نقش‌ها را فهرست می‌کند و بعد قدم‌های عملی را. نقش‌ها به همان ترتیب سؤال‌ها می‌آیند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-l2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L2-volunteer"],"often":{"pattern":"L2-volunteer","n":5,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 5 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 5’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۵ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A talk for new volunteers","tr":"Yeni gönüllüler için bir konuşma","fa":"صحبتی برای داوطلب‌های تازه"},"asks":{"en":"An organiser describes several volunteer roles, one after another, and then gives practical information: why help is needed, what volunteers enjoy, what you must do first and how to apply.","tr":"Bir organizatör birkaç gönüllü görevini birbiri ardına anlatıyor, sonra pratik bilgiler veriyor: neden yardıma ihtiyaç var, gönüllüler neden hoşlanıyor, önce ne yapmalısın ve nasıl başvurursun.","fa":"یک برگزارکننده چند نقش داوطلبانه را یکی پس از دیگری توصیف می‌کند و بعد اطلاعات عملی می‌دهد: چرا کمک لازم است، داوطلب‌ها از چه چیزی لذت می‌برند، اول چه باید بکنی و چطور درخواست بدهی."},"fields":["Each role and what it involves","Why more volunteers are needed","What volunteers enjoy","What everyone must do","How to apply"],"words":[{"a":"teenagers","b":"young people in their teens","tr":"gençler","fa":"نوجوان‌ها"},{"a":"older people","b":"pensioners / people in their seventies and eighties","tr":"yaşlılar","fa":"سالمندها"},{"a":"own transport","b":"you have to be able to drive yourself there","tr":"kendi aracın","fa":"وسیله‌ی نقلیه‌ی شخصی"},{"a":"work alone","b":"on your own / with nobody else around","tr":"yalnız çalışmak","fa":"تنها کار کردن"},{"a":"at weekends","b":"on Saturdays or Sundays","tr":"hafta sonları","fa":"آخر هفته‌ها"},{"a":"trained by a specialist","b":"a course with a professional","tr":"bir uzman tarafından eğitilmek","fa":"آموزش‌دیده توسط متخصص"},{"a":"commit","b":"promise to stay for a fixed time","tr":"taahhüt etmek","fa":"متعهد شدن"},{"a":"induction","b":"an introduction session before you start","tr":"oryantasyon","fa":"جلسه‌ی آشنایی"},{"a":"references","b":"letters from people who know you","tr":"referanslar","fa":"معرفی‌نامه"},{"a":"expert","b":"someone with a lot of technical knowledge","tr":"uzman","fa":"کارشناس، متخصص"}],"traps":[{"en":"In the matching task, each role often mentions two options from the box. One is ruled out: \"People assume you need X, but...\"","tr":"Eşleştirmede her görev çoğu zaman kutudan iki seçeneğe değinir. Biri elenir: \"İnsanlar X gerektiğini sanıyor ama...\"","fa":"در تمرین جورکردن، هر نقش اغلب به دو گزینه از کادر اشاره می‌کند. یکی رد می‌شود: «مردم فکر می‌کنند X لازم است، اما...»."},{"en":"\"Choose SIX answers from the box\": each letter is used once, and three letters are not used. Cross out letters as you use them.","tr":"\"Kutudan ALTI cevap seç\": her harf bir kez kullanılır ve üç harf kullanılmaz. Kullandıkça harflerin üstünü çiz.","fa":"«از کادر شش جواب انتخاب کن»: هر حرف یک بار به کار می‌رود و سه حرف استفاده نمی‌شوند. حرف‌ها را وقتی استفاده کردی خط بزن."},{"en":"A reason that is denied: \"It isn’t because... The reason is that...\" The second reason is the answer.","tr":"Reddedilen bir neden: \"Bunun nedeni ... değil. Nedeni şu ki...\" İkinci neden cevaptır.","fa":"دلیلی که رد می‌شود: «به‌خاطر ... نیست. دلیلش این است که...». دلیل دوم جواب است."}],"example":{"lines":[["Organiser","For the garden team, people think you need to know a lot about plants. You don’t. What you do need is to be free on Friday afternoons, because that’s when the team meets."]],"item":"Garden team: A needs plant knowledge  B available on a weekday afternoon","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Plant knowledge is ruled out (\"You don’t\"). \"Free on Friday afternoons\" = available on a weekday afternoon.","tr":"Bitki bilgisi eleniyor (\"Gerekmez\"). \"Cuma öğleden sonraları boş olmak\" = hafta içi bir öğleden sonra müsait olmak.","fa":"دانش گیاهی رد می‌شود («لازم نیست»). «جمعه بعدازظهرها آزاد بودن» یعنی یک بعدازظهر وسط هفته در دسترس بودن."}}},{"id":"L2-volunteer","ctx":["L2-volunteer"],"title":{"en":"Volunteering","tr":"Gönüllülük","fa":"کار داوطلبانه"},"asks":{"en":"An organiser describes volunteer work for a charity, a town or a company: what volunteers do, the training, the time needed and what they get in return.","tr":"Bir organizatör bir yardım kuruluşu, bir kasaba ya da bir şirket için gönüllü çalışmayı anlatır: gönüllülerin ne yaptığı, eğitim, gereken zaman ve karşılığında ne aldıkları.","fa":"یک برگزارکننده کار داوطلبانه برای یک خیریه، یک شهر یا یک شرکت را توضیح می‌دهد: داوطلب‌ها چه می‌کنند، آموزش، وقتی که لازم است و چیزی که در عوض می‌گیرند."},"fields":["What do most volunteers do?","What must new volunteers do first?","How much time do volunteers need to give?","Which TWO benefits are mentioned?","What does each role involve?"],"words":[{"a":"commitment","b":"how much time you give","tr":"ayırman gereken zaman","fa":"تعهد زمانی"},{"a":"role","b":"the job you'd do","tr":"görev","fa":"نقش"},{"a":"background check","b":"we check your history first","tr":"sicil kontrolü","fa":"بررسی سوابق"},{"a":"fundraising","b":"collecting money","tr":"bağış toplama","fa":"جمع‌آوری پول"},{"a":"expenses","b":"we pay your travel costs","tr":"masraflar","fa":"هزینه‌ها"},{"a":"no experience needed","b":"you don't need to have done it before","tr":"deneyim gerekmez","fa":"تجربه لازم نیست"},{"a":"flexible","b":"you choose your own hours","tr":"esnek","fa":"منعطف"},{"a":"community","b":"local people / the town","tr":"topluluk","fa":"جامعه‌ی محلی"},{"a":"in return","b":"what you get back","tr":"karşılığında","fa":"در عوض"},{"a":"regular","b":"every week","tr":"düzenli","fa":"منظم"},{"a":"reference","b":"a letter for job applications","tr":"referans mektubu","fa":"توصیه‌نامه"},{"a":"at short notice","b":"at the last minute","tr":"son dakikada","fa":"با خبر کوتاه"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"No experience needed\" is said about one role but not about another.","tr":"\"Deneyim gerekmez\" bir görev için söylenir, diğeri için değil.","fa":"«تجربه لازم نیست» درباره‌ی یک نقش گفته می‌شود، نه درباره‌ی نقش دیگر."},{"en":"Benefits: one option was true in the past (\"we used to give...\") and is not true now.","tr":"Faydalar: bir seçenek geçmişte doğruydu (\"eskiden ... verirdik\") ama artık değil.","fa":"مزایا: یکی از گزینه‌ها قبلاً درست بود («قبلاً ... می‌دادیم») ولی حالا نیست."}],"example":{"lines":[["Organiser","You don’t need any special skills to help in the shop."],["Organiser","Drivers, though, must have held a licence for at least three years."],["Organiser","They don’t need to have driven a van before."]],"item":"What do drivers need?  A experience in a shop   B a licence held for three years   C van-driving experience","answer":"B","why":{"en":"\"Though\" moves from the shop to drivers. Van experience is ruled out.","tr":"\"Though\" dükkândan sürücülere geçiyor. Kamyonet deneyimi eleniyor.","fa":"«Though» از مغازه به راننده‌ها می‌رود. تجربه‌ی رانندگی ون رد می‌شود."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L2-volunteer"],"often":{"pattern":"L2-volunteer","n":5,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 5 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 5’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۵ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"A box of nine, then four A-C questions","tr":"Dokuzluk bir kutu, sonra dört A-C sorusu","fa":"یک کادر نُه‌تایی، بعد چهار سؤال A-C"},"body":{"en":"Questions 11-16: six roles and a box of nine statements, A-I. Choose SIX answers: each letter is used once and three are left over. Questions 17-20: choose A, B or C. You read Questions 11-16 first and Questions 17-20 in the break.","tr":"Soru 11-16: altı görev ve A-I arası dokuz ifadelik bir kutu. ALTI cevap seç: her harf bir kez kullanılır, üçü artar. Soru 17-20: A, B ya da C’yi seç. Önce Soru 11-16’yı, molada Soru 17-20’yi okursun.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۱ تا ۱۶: شش نقش و کادری با نُه جمله، A تا I. شش جواب انتخاب کن: هر حرف یک بار و سه تا اضافه می‌مانند. سؤال‌های ۱۷ تا ۲۰: A، B یا C را انتخاب کن. اول سؤال‌های ۱۱ تا ۱۶ را می‌خوانی و در وقفه ۱۷ تا ۲۰ را."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Know the box before you listen","tr":"Dinlemeden önce kutuyu tanı","fa":"قبل از گوش دادن کادر را بشناس"},"steps":[{"en":"In the reading time, put each box statement into two or three key words: teenagers, own car, alone.","tr":"Okuma süresinde her kutu ifadesini iki üç anahtar kelimeye indir: teenagers, own car, alone.","fa":"در وقت خواندن، هر جمله‌ی کادر را به دو سه کلیدواژه تبدیل کن: teenagers، own car، alone."},{"en":"Listen for the name of each role: it tells you which question you are on.","tr":"Her görevin adını dinle: hangi sorudasın, o söyler.","fa":"به اسم هر نقش گوش بده: می‌گوید روی کدام سؤالی."},{"en":"Wait for the end of each role: the first option you hear is often ruled out.","tr":"Her görevin sonunu bekle: duyduğun ilk seçenek çoğu zaman elenir.","fa":"تا آخر توضیح هر نقش صبر کن: اولین گزینه‌ای که می‌شنوی اغلب رد می‌شود."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Two options in one role","tr":"Bir görevde iki seçenek","fa":"دو گزینه در یک نقش"},"body":{"en":"The speaker often mentions a wrong option first and then corrects it: \"People assume you need computer skills... but what you’ll be doing is...\" Use a letter only for what the speaker says is true of the role.","tr":"Konuşan çoğu zaman önce yanlış bir seçenekten söz eder, sonra düzeltir: \"İnsanlar bilgisayar becerisi gerektiğini sanıyor... ama yapacağın şey...\" Bir harfi yalnızca konuşanın o görev için doğru dediği şey için kullan.","fa":"گوینده اغلب اول یک گزینه‌ی غلط را می‌گوید و بعد اصلاحش می‌کند: «مردم فکر می‌کنند مهارت کامپیوتر لازم است... اما کاری که انجام می‌دهی...». فقط برای چیزی حرف بگذار که گوینده درباره‌ی آن نقش درست می‌داند."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One role, step by step","tr":"Bir görev, adım adım","fa":"یک نقش، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"What does the organiser say about each role? Choose from the box.","item":"Reception desk · A You need to speak another language.  B You must be available early in the morning.","lines":[["Organiser","Volunteers on reception sometimes worry that they need a second language. Most visitors speak English, so that’s not a problem. But the desk opens at seven, so you have to be an early riser."]],"answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"The role name, \"reception\", tells you which question this is.","tr":"Görev adı, \"reception\", hangi soru olduğunu söylüyor.","fa":"اسم نقش، «reception»، می‌گوید کدام سؤال است."},{"en":"A is mentioned and ruled out: \"that’s not a problem\".","tr":"A geçiyor ve eleniyor: \"sorun değil\".","fa":"A گفته و رد می‌شود: «مشکلی نیست»."},{"en":"\"The desk opens at seven... an early riser\" = available early in the morning: B.","tr":"\"Masa yedide açılıyor... erken kalkan biri\" = sabah erken müsait: B.","fa":"«میز ساعت هفت باز می‌شود... سحرخیز» یعنی صبح زود در دسترس: B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"It’s not because the building is old. We’re closing for two weeks because the heating is being replaced.\" Why is the place closing?","options":["because the building is old","for the summer holidays","to replace the heating"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The age of the building is denied; \"because the heating is being replaced\" is the reason.","tr":"Binanın eskiliği reddediliyor; \"çünkü ısıtma sistemi değiştiriliyor\" asıl neden.","fa":"قدیمی بودن ساختمان رد می‌شود؛ «چون سیستم گرمایش عوض می‌شود» دلیل اصلی است."}},"remember":{"en":"Learn the box before the talk, wait for the end of each role, and cross out each letter once you have used it.","tr":"Konuşmadan önce kutuyu öğren, her görevin sonunu bekle ve kullandığın harfin üstünü çiz.","fa":"قبل از صحبت کادر را یاد بگیر، تا آخر هر نقش صبر کن و هر حرفی را که استفاده کردی خط بزن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-l2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-l2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 2","title":{"en":"Volunteering at Kingsmead Central Library","tr":"Kingsmead Merkez Kütüphanesi’nde gönüllülük","fa":"داوطلبی در کتابخانه‌ی مرکزی کینگزمید"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L2-volunteer"],"script":[{"who":"Organiser","line":"Good evening, everyone, and thank you for coming. My name's Teresa Quayle, and I organise the volunteers here at Kingsmead Central Library. Tonight I'm going to tell you about the different ways you can help us, and then I'll explain what happens next if you decide to join."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"Let's start with our homework club. It runs on weekday afternoons from half past three, and it's for young people aged thirteen to sixteen who need a quiet place to study and a bit of support. A lot of people assume you need to be good with computers for this, because the students use our laptops, but honestly they know far more about the technology than we do. What you'll be doing is sitting with teenagers and helping them organise their work. Some of them have nowhere quiet to study at home, and just having an adult who notices whether they turn up can make a big difference."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"Then there's our digital drop-in, on Tuesday mornings. This is where people come for help with things like booking a doctor's appointment online or video-calling their grandchildren. Almost everyone who comes is over seventy. You don't need to be an expert, by the way. Patience matters far more than technical knowledge."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"Our home library service delivers books to people who can't get to the library themselves, mostly because of illness. Volunteers choose books with each reader on the phone and then take them round every three weeks. The routes cover the villages outside the city, where there are no buses at all, so for this one you'd need to have your own car."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"Next, the local history archive. We have thousands of old photographs of the city that have never been catalogued. Volunteers sort them, write short descriptions and scan them for our website. It's fascinating, but I should warn you that the archive is in the basement and it's very quiet work. Most of the time it's just you and the photographs."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"The conversation café is for people who've recently moved to the city and want to practise their English. People often ask whether they need to speak other languages to help. You don't: the whole point is to speak English, slowly and clearly. The café meets on Saturday mornings, so it suits people who work during the week."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"And finally, storytime for toddlers. This is the most popular session we run, with up to forty children and their parents. Reading a picture book aloud to a room full of two-year-olds is harder than it looks, so before you start, you'll do a half-day course with a professional storyteller, who shows you how to use your voice and keep the children's attention. Parents tell us it's often the only time in the week when they can sit and enjoy a book with their child without any interruptions."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"Right, now a few general points. Some of you have asked why we need so many new volunteers this year. It isn't because we're losing staff. In fact, the council has just agreed to keep all our jobs. The reason is that from April the library will open on Sundays as well, and we need people to help run activities on that extra day."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"I asked our current volunteers what they get out of it. Some mentioned learning new skills, and quite a few said they'd made new friends. But the thing almost everyone wrote down was that they feel useful, that what they do makes a real difference to someone."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"Before you start, there's one thing that everyone must do, whichever role you choose, and that's come to an induction evening. The next one is on the fourteenth of March. References, by the way, are only needed for roles with children, and there's no uniform, just a name badge that we'll give you."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"As for applying, we did have an online form, but it's been causing problems, so for now please pick up a paper application form from the information desk on your way out. And we don't ask you to commit for a fixed time. If you can give us three months, that's wonderful."},{"who":"Organiser","line":"So, thank you again. I'll be here for another half an hour if you have any questions."}],"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 11-16. What does the organiser say about each of the following volunteer roles? Choose SIX answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-I, next to Questions 11-16.","qtype":"matching","bank":["A You need to be free at weekends.","B You need your own transport.","C You will work mainly with older people.","D You must stay for at least a year.","E You need to speak another language.","F You will usually work alone.","G You need good computer skills.","H You will be trained by a specialist.","I You will work with teenagers."],"questions":[{"n":11,"kind":"match","prompt":"homework club","correct":8,"evidence":"What you'll be doing is sitting with teenagers","why":{"en":"Computer skills are ruled out (\"they know far more about the technology than we do\"). Volunteers sit \"with teenagers\": I.","tr":"Bilgisayar becerisi eleniyor (\"teknolojiyi bizden çok daha iyi biliyorlar\"). Gönüllüler \"gençlerle\" oturuyor: I.","fa":"مهارت کامپیوتر رد می‌شود («از ما خیلی بیشتر درباره‌ی فناوری می‌دانند»). داوطلب‌ها «کنار نوجوان‌ها» می‌نشینند: I."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"match","prompt":"digital drop-in","correct":2,"evidence":"Almost everyone who comes is over seventy","why":{"en":"\"Almost everyone who comes is over seventy\" = mainly older people. Expert skills are not needed (G).","tr":"\"Gelenlerin neredeyse hepsi yetmiş yaşın üstünde\" = çoğunlukla yaşlılar. Uzman becerisi gerekmiyor (G).","fa":"«تقریباً همه‌ی کسانی که می‌آیند بالای هفتاد سال‌اند» یعنی بیشتر سالمندها. مهارت تخصصی لازم نیست (G)."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"match","prompt":"home library service","correct":1,"evidence":"for this one you'd need to have your own car","why":{"en":"There are no buses to the villages, so \"you’d need to have your own car\" = own transport.","tr":"Köylere otobüs yok, bu yüzden \"kendi arabanın olması gerekir\" = kendi aracın.","fa":"به روستاها اتوبوس نمی‌رود، پس «باید ماشین خودت را داشته باشی» یعنی وسیله‌ی نقلیه‌ی شخصی."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"local history archive","correct":5,"evidence":"Most of the time it's just you and the photographs","why":{"en":"\"Most of the time it’s just you and the photographs\" = working alone.","tr":"\"Çoğu zaman sadece sen ve fotoğraflar varsınız\" = yalnız çalışmak.","fa":"«بیشتر وقت‌ها فقط خودت هستی و عکس‌ها» یعنی تنها کار کردن."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":15,"kind":"match","prompt":"conversation café","correct":0,"evidence":"The café meets on Saturday mornings","why":{"en":"Another language is ruled out (\"You don’t\"). It \"meets on Saturday mornings\" = at weekends.","tr":"Başka bir dil eleniyor (\"Gerekmez\"). \"Cumartesi sabahları toplanıyor\" = hafta sonları.","fa":"زبان دیگر رد می‌شود («لازم نیست»). «شنبه صبح‌ها برگزار می‌شود» یعنی آخر هفته."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"match","prompt":"storytime for toddlers","correct":7,"evidence":"a half-day course with a professional storyteller","why":{"en":"\"A half-day course with a professional storyteller\" = trained by a specialist.","tr":"\"Profesyonel bir masalcıyla yarım günlük bir kurs\" = bir uzman tarafından eğitilmek.","fa":"«یک دوره‌ی نیم‌روزه با یک قصه‌گوی حرفه‌ای» یعنی آموزش از یک متخصص."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 17-20. Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":17,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why does the library need more volunteers this year?","options":["A It will open on an extra day each week.","B It has lost several members of staff.","C It is moving to a larger building."],"correct":0,"evidence":"from April the library will open on Sundays as well","why":{"en":"\"It isn’t because we’re losing staff.\" The reason: \"from April the library will open on Sundays as well\".","tr":"\"Personel kaybettiğimiz için değil.\" Neden: \"Nisandan itibaren kütüphane pazar günleri de açık olacak\".","fa":"«به‌خاطر از دست دادن کارمند نیست». دلیل: «از آوریل کتابخانه یکشنبه‌ها هم باز است»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What do almost all current volunteers say they get from the work?","options":["A new skills","B new friends","C a sense of being useful"],"correct":2,"evidence":"the thing almost everyone wrote down was that they feel useful","why":{"en":"\"Some\" mentioned skills and \"quite a few\" friends, but \"almost everyone\" said they feel useful.","tr":"\"Bazıları\" becerilerden, \"epeycesi\" arkadaşlardan söz etti ama \"neredeyse herkes\" işe yaradığını hissettiğini yazdı.","fa":"«بعضی‌ها» از مهارت و «تعداد زیادی» از دوست گفتند، اما «تقریباً همه» نوشتند احساس مفید بودن می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":19,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What must every new volunteer do before starting?","options":["A provide references","B attend an evening meeting","C collect a uniform"],"correct":1,"evidence":"that's come to an induction evening","why":{"en":"References are \"only needed for roles with children\", and there is \"no uniform\". Everyone must \"come to an induction evening\".","tr":"Referanslar \"yalnızca çocuklarla ilgili görevler için gerekli\" ve \"üniforma yok\". Herkes \"bir oryantasyon akşamına gelmeli\".","fa":"معرفی‌نامه «فقط برای نقش‌های مربوط به بچه‌ها لازم است» و «یونیفرمی در کار نیست». همه باید «در یک عصرِ آشنایی شرکت کنند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"How should people apply at the moment?","options":["A by using the online form","B by collecting a form from the library","C by telephoning the organiser"],"correct":1,"evidence":"please pick up a paper application form from the information desk","why":{"en":"The online form \"has been causing problems\". For now, \"pick up a paper application form from the information desk\".","tr":"Çevrim içi form \"sorun çıkarıyor\". Şimdilik \"bilgi masasından kâğıt bir başvuru formu alın\".","fa":"فرم آنلاین «مشکل درست کرده». فعلاً «یک فرم کاغذی از میز اطلاعات بردار»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Organiser":{"accent":"North American","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"af_sarah"},"role":"Volunteer organiser at the library"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 2. You will hear a woman talking to a group of people who want to become volunteers at a city library. First, you have some time to look at Questions 11 to 16."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 11-16"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 11 to 16."},{"type":"sfx","note":"small meeting room, light murmur before the speaker begins"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":6},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at Questions 17 to 20."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 17-20"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 17 to 20."},{"type":"lines","from":7,"to":11},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x06-l2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-l2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Everyone must come to an induction evening.\" An induction is...","options":["a party at the end of the year","a session that introduces new people to the job","a test you must pass"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"An induction introduces new staff or volunteers to how things work.","tr":"Oryantasyon, yeni çalışanları ya da gönüllüleri işin nasıl yürüdüğüyle tanıştırır.","fa":"جلسه‌ی آشنایی، کارمندها یا داوطلب‌های تازه را با روند کار آشنا می‌کند."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A box option says \"You will usually work alone.\" Which words in a talk mean the same?","options":["most of the time it’s just you","you’ll be part of a big team","you’ll work with a partner"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Just you\" most of the time = usually alone.","tr":"Çoğu zaman \"sadece sen\" = genelde yalnız.","fa":"بیشتر وقت‌ها «فقط خودت» یعنی معمولاً تنها."}},{"tests":"method","point":1,"prompt":"\"Choose SIX answers from the box\" with a box of nine letters. What do you do after using a letter?","options":["Keep it: it may come back","Use it for the next question too","Cross it out: it will not be used again"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Each letter is used once, so crossing out used letters makes the choice smaller.","tr":"Her harf bir kez kullanılır; kullanılanların üstünü çizmek seçimi daraltır.","fa":"هر حرف یک بار به کار می‌رود، پس خط زدن حرف‌های استفاده‌شده انتخاب را راحت‌تر می‌کند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"People think you need to be good at maths for the shop. You don’t. What you really need is a friendly manner.\" Which option fits the shop?","options":["You need to be good at maths.","You need to be friendly.","You need retail experience."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Maths is ruled out (\"You don’t\"); \"what you really need\" gives the answer.","tr":"Matematik eleniyor (\"Gerekmez\"); \"asıl gereken\" cevabı veriyor.","fa":"ریاضی رد می‌شود («لازم نیست»)؛ «چیزی که واقعاً لازم داری» جواب را می‌دهد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":2,"prompt":"\"Some volunteers said they enjoyed the training. But nearly all of them said the best thing was meeting new people.\" What do most volunteers enjoy most?","options":["meeting new people","the training","the free lunches"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Some\" vs \"nearly all\": the question asks about most volunteers.","tr":"\"Bazıları\" ile \"neredeyse hepsi\": soru çoğu gönüllüyü soruyor.","fa":"«بعضی‌ها» در برابر «تقریباً همه»: سؤال درباره‌ی بیشترِ داوطلب‌هاست."}}],"id":"c-x06-l2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-l2"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
